# React Standards (React 18+)

## Component Model
- Use functional components only.
- Prefer Hooks-first patterns; avoid class components.
- Keep components small and focused on a single responsibility.
- Components must be pure with predictable inputs/outputs.

## TypeScript & Props
- Prefer TypeScript for components and hooks.
- Use explicit prop types; avoid implicit `any`.
- Prefer discriminated unions for variant props.
- Define `Props` as a named type; avoid inline complex types.

## File & Folder Conventions
- Co-locate component files with styles and tests.
- Keep shared UI in `components/` and domain UI in `features/<domain>/`.
- Export public components via index files only.
- Prefer one component per file.

## Accessibility & Performance
- Enforce semantic HTML and accessible labels.
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders; memoize only when justified.
- Use lazy loading for large routes or heavy components.
- Use `aria-*` attributes only when semantics are insufficient.
